#METABOLOMICS WORKBENCH AS_Restriction_20260209_002402 DATATRACK_ID:7103 STUDY_ID:ST004848 ANALYSIS_ID:AN008205 PROJECT_ID:PR003093
VERSION             	1
CREATED_ON             	May 15, 2026, 1:16 pm
#PROJECT
PR:PROJECT_TITLE                 	Metabolic silencing via methionine-based amino acid restriction in multiple
PR:PROJECT_TITLE                 	myeloma cell line MPC11 induced low energy metabolism
PR:PROJECT_TYPE                  	LC-MS
PR:PROJECT_SUMMARY               	In our laboratory, the MPC11 murine cell line served as a model system for
PR:PROJECT_SUMMARY               	Methionine Restriction (MetR). For proof of principle, liquid
PR:PROJECT_SUMMARY               	chromatography/mass spectrometry (LC–MS) was performed to generate a metabolic
PR:PROJECT_SUMMARY               	profile (metabolic fingerprint) of MetR (0.5 mg/L) every 24 h over a five-day
PR:PROJECT_SUMMARY               	period. More than 170 metabolites derived from amino acids through glycolysis
PR:PROJECT_SUMMARY               	and the tricarboxylic acid (TCA) and urea cycles and from purines, pyrimidines,
PR:PROJECT_SUMMARY               	etc., were examined to demonstrate the effects of MetR at the metabolic level.
PR:PROJECT_SUMMARY               	The experiments were conducted three times, and the results were subsequently
PR:PROJECT_SUMMARY               	summarized.
PR:INSTITUTE                     	Universitätsklinikum Würzburg
PR:DEPARTMENT                    	Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Plastic Surgery
PR:LABORATORY                    	MKG Forschung
PR:LAST_NAME                     	Seher
PR:FIRST_NAME                    	Axel
PR:ADDRESS                       	Pleicherwall 2, Wuerzburg, Bavaria, 97074, Germany
