PR:PUBLICATIONS                  	bioRxiv 2025.08.17.670755; doi: https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.08.17.670755
#STUDY
ST:STUDY_TITLE                   	Metabolic silencing via methionine-based amino acid restriction in murine
ST:STUDY_TITLE                   	multiple myeloma cell line MPC11 induced low energy and reduced nucleotide
ST:STUDY_TITLE                   	metabolism
ST:STUDY_TYPE                    	LC-MS
ST:STUDY_SUMMARY                 	In this work, we analysed Amino Acid Restriction implemented via methionine
ST:STUDY_SUMMARY                 	restriction (MetR) in the MPC11 murine cell line. MetR exerted profound
ST:STUDY_SUMMARY                 	antiproliferative effects without causing cell death. Mass spectrometry analyses
ST:STUDY_SUMMARY                 	of MPC11 cells revealed metabolic reprogramming, indicating that MetR led to a
ST:STUDY_SUMMARY                 	dramatic decrease in the (aerobic) glycolysis rate and in the abundances of
ST:STUDY_SUMMARY                 	energy equivalents and nucleotide synthesis metabolites.
ST:INSTITUTE                     	Universitätsklinikum Würzburg
ST:DEPARTMENT                    	Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Plastic Surgery
ST:LABORATORY                    	MKG Forschung
