#COLLECTION
CO:COLLECTION_SUMMARY            	Refer to the treatment summary for details regarding cell culture and collection
CO:COLLECTION_SUMMARY            	of the Murine MPC11 cell line, B lymphocyte cell line of a mouse with
CO:COLLECTION_SUMMARY            	plasmacytoma.
CO:SAMPLE_TYPE                   	B-cells
#TREATMENT
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	A total of 2x10^6 MPC11 cells were seeded in 25 mL of medium in 15 cm Petri
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	dishes, and every value was measured on the basis of a 30 mg/L L-methionine
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	control and 0.5 mg/L L-methionine for Met(-) and incubated for 24 h, 48 h, 72 h,
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	96 h and 120 h. Because a small fraction of the cells died over a 120 h period
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	under complete methionine deprivation, a small amount of methionine was added to
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	the Met(-)-medium for the mass spectrometry experiment. The cells were removed
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	from the Petri dishes with a cell scraper. The pellets were produced via
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	centrifugation at 1500xg for 5 min. The cells were resuspended in the
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	appropriate medium, and the cell number was determined in every sample at four
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	different times to obtain an accurate number of cells. A total of 1x106 cells
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	were transferred to a 1.5-mL Eppendorf tube and centrifuged at 18000xg for 5
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	min. The supernatant was removed, and until LC–MS analysis, the pellets were
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	stored at -20 °C. The experiment was performed three times.
#SAMPLEPREP
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	After the addition of 0.5 mL of MeOH/CH3CN/H2O (50/30/20, v/v/v) containing 10
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	µM lamivudine, the cell pellets were homogenized via ultrasonication (10*1 s at
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	250 W output energy). The external standard lamivudine was not used for absolute
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	metabolite quantification but was used as a quality control to compensate for
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	inevitable technical issues. For quality control and determination of the
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	corresponding retention times, most of the annotated metabolites (which are
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	commercially available) were run as mixtures of pure compounds under identical
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	experimental conditions. General procedure: The resulting suspension was
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	centrifuged (20 kRCF for 2 min in an Eppendorf centrifuge 5424), and the
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	supernatant was loaded onto a C18-SPE column that was activated with 0.5 mL of
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	CH3CN and equilibrated with 0.5 mL of MeOH/CH3CN/H2O (50/30/20, v/v/v). The
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	solid-phase eluate (SPE) was evaporated under vacuum. The resulting pellet was
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	dissolved in 50 µL of cell extract in 5 mM NH4OAc in CH3CN/(25%/75%, v/v).
#CHROMATOGRAPHY
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_SUMMARY        	Mobile phase A consisted of 5 mM NH4OAc in CH3CN/H2O (5/95, v/v), and mobile
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_SUMMARY        	phase B consisted of 5 mM NH4OAc in CH3CN/H2O (95/5, v/v). After the sample was
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_SUMMARY        	loaded onto a ZIC-HILIC column (at 30 °C), the following LC gradient programme
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_SUMMARY        	was applied: 100% solvent B for 2 min, a linear decrease to 40% solvent B within
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_SUMMARY        	16 min, maintenance at 40% solvent B for 9 min, and an increase to 100% solvent
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_SUMMARY        	B within 1 min. The column was maintained at 100% solvent B for 5 min for column
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_SUMMARY        	equilibration before each injection. The flow rate was maintained at 200
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_SUMMARY        	μL/min. The eluent was directed to the electrospray ionization (ESI) source of
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_SUMMARY        	a Q Exactive (QE)-mass spectrometer from 1.85 min to 20.0 min after sample
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_SUMMARY        	injection.
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_TYPE           	HILIC
CH:INSTRUMENT_NAME               	Thermo Dionex Ultimate 3000
CH:COLUMN_NAME                   	Sequant ZIC-HILIC (100 x 2.1 mm, 2.5 um)
CH:SOLVENT_A                     	5% acetonitrile/95% water; 5 mM ammonium acetate
CH:SOLVENT_B                     	95% acetonitrile/5% water; 5 mM ammonium acetate
CH:FLOW_GRADIENT                 	100% solvent B for 2 min, a linear decrease to 40% solvent B within 16 min,
CH:FLOW_GRADIENT                 	maintenance at 40% solvent B for 9 min, and an increase to 100% solvent B within
CH:FLOW_GRADIENT                 	1 min. The column was maintained at 100% solvent B for 5 min for column
CH:FLOW_GRADIENT                 	equilibration before each injection.
CH:FLOW_RATE                     	200 μL/min
CH:COLUMN_TEMPERATURE            	30 °C
#ANALYSIS
AN:ANALYSIS_TYPE                 	MS
#MS
MS:INSTRUMENT_NAME               	Thermo Q Exactive Orbitrap
MS:INSTRUMENT_TYPE               	Orbitrap
MS:MS_TYPE                       	ESI
MS:ION_MODE                      	POSITIVE
